# oracle: w194gneb_chain — 8 spins on a periodic line (metal units, atom_style spin, spin/exchange J = 0.02726 eV between nearest
# neighbours 2.5 A apart, zeeman 0.1 eV along z, anisotropy 1e-4 eV along x) in 4 replicas: the neb/spin table (geodesic NEB,
# min_style spin, fix neb/spin 1.0, file-style final with Rodrigues interpolation of the intermediate spins). Tolerances 0 0:
# 60 regular and 60 climbing iterations, a row every 10; the climbing replica is replica 3 (interior).
# Measured with native LAMMPS: the engine's 14 table rows equal native's at the table's printed precision (8 significant
# digits, %12.8g of print_status): max relative error 0 after rounding the engine value the same way; unrounded, the largest
# difference is 4.7e-8 (MaxAtomTorque), the printed digits themselves. The per-iteration spins and forces of all four replicas
# agree with native's dumps to 3e-10 (dump precision). Engine 1.6 s.
# native: b332f28 (the installed lmp, SPIN and REPLICA packages)
# oracle-partitions: 4
# oracle-inputs: w194gneb_chain.data w194gneb_chain.final
# oracle-compare: rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 printed=8
units metal
dimension 3
boundary p p p
atom_style spin
atom_modify map array
read_data w194gneb_chain.data
mass 1 55.845
pair_style spin/exchange 3.0
pair_coeff * * exchange 3.0 0.02726 0.2171 1.841
neighbor 0.1 bin
neigh_modify every 10 check yes delay 20
fix 1 all precession/spin zeeman 0.1 0.0 0.0 1.0 anisotropy 0.0001 1.0 0.0 0.0
fix_modify 1 energy yes
fix 3 all neb/spin 1.0
timestep 0.0001
thermo 10
thermo_style custom step pe
thermo_modify format float %.15g
min_style spin
min_modify alpha_damp 1.0 discrete_factor 10.0
neb/spin 0.0 0.0 60 60 10 final w194gneb_chain.final
